<!--
  Stereo Eye - a cute 2-wheel differential-drive mapping robot.
  One "eye" that is a calibrated 2-camera stereo pair (80 mm baseline, 640x360 per eye @ 24 fps,
  identical intrinsics) on a rigid stereo bar, for RTAB-Map stereo SLAM and navigation.
  See ../STEREO_DESIGN.md for the camera design rationale.

  Frames (REP-105 / REP-103):
    base_footprint -> base_link -> {left,right}_wheel_link (continuous)
                                -> caster_link (fixed, rear)
                                -> front_caster_link (fixed, front skid/caster)
                                -> front_tof_link (fixed, short-range ToF / gpu_lidar)
                                -> ballast_link (fixed, low battery pack)
                                -> imu_link (fixed)
                                -> head_link (fixed) -> stereo_bar_link (fixed, rigid stereo bar)
                                                          -> camera_link (stereo centre)
                                                          -> camera_left_link  -> camera_left_optical_frame
                                                          -> camera_right_link -> camera_right_optical_frame
  Visuals use primitives only (box / cylinder / sphere) so no meshes are needed.
-->
